(A map parameter given a `value` holding a map receives a copy of the map.
 A list parameter given the same `value` is not called: it does not hold a
 list, so the error flag is set.)
a value called box is {"pears": 1}.
To 'stock up' with a map called shelf.
    Set shelf's "plums" to 2.
    Print "shelf: {shelf}".

To 'count' with a list called items.
    Print "items: {items's length}".

'stock up' of box.
Print "box: {box}".
'count' of box.
On error print "not a list: the call was skipped".
Print "box: {box}".
